I recently played a wizard and thought you might be
interested in the details of his demise.

When I started, I first went to Minetown to find a
coaligned altar. Of course, I started sacrificing
corpses until Thoth gave me Magicbane, which I already
was quite content with. On the way out, I met some
monsters to test Magicbane on; Thoth seemed to like me
as he rewarded me with Vorpal Blade.

This made the rest of the game much easier after I had
enchanted it to +3. Sadly I didn't find a container at
all and the SDSM I got from a magic lamp in Minetown
made me just leave Sokoban alone once I realized it
would only have an amulet of reflection for me. Still,
I bought some protection with the gold from a leprechaun
hall.

Finally I arrived on Medusa's level. Looking at the
purple H I knew this wouldn't be fun, so I engraved
Elbereth. Over and over again.
A bit to the south a gremlin had started to multiply,
but I didn't care; I was too busy fighting the monsters
the titan summoned.

Vorpal Blade quickly killed most of the monsters
(especially the two jabberwocks, of course) while
I was safe on my E square.

Then, the titan summoned a captain with a silver saber.
I should have noticed, but I somehow didn't.

After running upstairs, he followed me and killed me directly
on the level above Medusa's. Looking back, my ring of
regeneration might have saved me if I noticed the captain
earlier.

Well, let's be optimistic, maybe someone on NAO enjoys
a (probably cursed) +3 Vorpal Blade now :)

